jobs.description:
Ready for a job full of action? Come work at Wasco in Deventer! As a warehouse worker, you’ll work in various departments. Stay active and earn up to €24,32 per hour.

For this function you will need your own housing in the Netherlands. Unfortunately we do not offer housing with this job. Apply now and get a WhatsApp message within 15 minutes with questions so we can help you quickly. Do not have a WhatsApp? Then we will contact you by phone or email!

What we offer
- Amazing salary starting at €16,21 per hour
- Travel expenses? Covered!
- Earn up to €24,32 per hour including bonuses
- Every weekend off! Yes, you read that right!
- Full-time? Part-time? YES!
- Fun activities & sing-along to the best hits

Who you are
To keep the Wasco warehouse running smoothly, it is important that you meet the following requirements as a warehouse worker:

-     You speak English, for safety reasons;    
- You are at least 18 years old, due to driving an EPT;    
- You are at least available to work on Mondays and Fridays (more days are possible);    
- You are available to work in different shifts. The working hours are from 09:00 to 18:00,    12:00 to 21:00 and 15:00 to 00.00;    
- You have your own transport to get to Deventer;    
- You are physically capable of lifting product weighing at least 20 kilos;    
- You agree that we can not offer a guarantee of hours.

What will you do
As a warehouse worker at Wasco in Deventer, no two days are the same. You can work in various departments, depending on what suits you best. For example, you might work in the receiving department. This is where you greet drivers, check deliveries, and handle the administrative paperwork. In the modern “autostore,” you’ll work with smart systems and pick small parts like screws and connectors. Prefer a more hands-on role? Then the order picker position is a good fit for you. You’ll pick larger products like bathtubs and radiators. As a warehouse worker, you’ll work Monday through Friday. If you’d prefer to work fewer

Are you an experienced Reach Truck Driver looking for a new opportunity? We are currently recruiting for a modern logistics company in Helmond. As a Reach Truck Driver, you will be responsible for safely and efficiently moving goods throughout the warehouse while supporting daily logistics operations using modern equipment.

Your responsibilities:

- Operating a reach truck at heights of up to 12 meters;
- Moving and storing pallets throughout the warehouse;
- Picking orders using the reach truck;
- Scanning, labeling, and wrapping pallets;
- Checking orders before shipment;
- Supporting Value Added Services (VAS) activities;
- Maintaining a clean, safe, and organized working environment.

Working Hours in the day shift: 07:00 AM – 04:00 PM. During peak periods in July till October, a two-shift schedule may be required. (6:00-15:00/15:00-00:00)

- Holds a valid Reach Truck certificate;
- Is comfortable working at heights up to 12 meters;
- Fulltime available;
- Living nearby Helmond, Mierlo, Geldrop, Nuenen or Eindhoven;
- Has experience in logistics and safety;
- Is flexible regarding tasks and working hours;
- Has a good command of Dutch and/or English.

Do you enjoy being active and seeing tangible results? Are you looking for a job where you can work more hours by working at different locations? Then this combined role is perfect for you!
We offer you the opportunity to work at both the Designer Outlet Center in Roermond and De Leistert vacation park in Roggel. By combining these two locations, you can expect a workweek of approximately 32 to 40 hours.

What will you be doing?

You’ll be working at two different locations, which ensures plenty of variety in your work:

Designer Outlet Center Roermond

- Cleaning streets and plazas with street sweepers and pressure washers;
- Emptying trash cans on the premises;
- Picking up litter;
- Ensuring a clean and well-maintained environment for visitors.

De Leistert Holiday Park (Roggel)

- Cleaning bungalows, vacation homes, and restroom facilities;
- Making beds;
- Cleaning kitchens, bathrooms, bedrooms, and living rooms;
- Dusting and mopping the accommodations;
- Identifying and reporting any defects.

This combination offers a varied job where you work both indoors and outdoors and see the immediate results of your work.

Work Hours

- Outlet Roermond: flexible availability, including weekends;
- De Leistert: Mondays and Fridays between 9:00 AM and 3:00 PM (alternating days) with the possibility of additional work during the week;
- A combination of both locations allows for a workweek of approximately 32 to 40 hours.

- You’re a go-getter and enjoy being active;
- You’re available for at least 15 hours per week;
- You’re flexible (including weekends for the outlet);
- You’re available on Mondays and Fridays (for De Leistert);
- You speak Dutch, English, or German;
- Experience in cleaning is a plus, but not required.

For our client in Kessel, we are looking for a production employee for the Maintenance and Laundry department. In this role, you’ll be responsible for inspecting used materials for quality, cleaning them, packaging, and getting them ready for transport or storage. You'll work with modern machinery to ensure the customer receives rental items that are complete, clean, and undamaged. You’ll be handling various tent components such as floors, walls, doors, windows, and canvases, cleaning them both manually and with machines. Familiarity with industrial machinery and using a high-pressure cleaner is essential.

Your tasks will include:

- Washing and maintaining tent components and rental materials (e.g., floors, walls, doors, windows, and canvases) by machine and hand;
- Operating industrial washers, dryers, high-pressure cleaners, and overhead cranes;
- Monitoring product quality and detecting any damages;
- Inspecting and packing canvases;
- Preparing materials for storage or transport;
- Maintaining a safe and sustainable workspace.

You will be working in an international environment where Dutch and English are the primary languages. Working hours are from 07:00 to 15:30, Monday through Friday.

We are seeking someone with experience in an industrial production setting and a hands-on approach. You’re not afraid to roll up your sleeves and tackle physical tasks. Additionally, you possess:

- A completed VMBO or basic vocational education (level 2) or an equivalent qualification;
- Good command of Dutch or English;
- A forklift certification, or you’re willing to obtain one;
- A desire to grow by participating in internal training opportunities.

Are you a hands-on worker, do you like working in an organized way, and do you feel at home in a logistics environment? Would you like to be part of one of Europe’s largest producers of custom-made sandwich panels? Then this position at our client in Waalwijk is perfect for you!

As a Logistics Employee, you play an important role in the logistics process surrounding the production of high-quality, custom-made sandwich panels for, among others, the bodywork industry and the defense sector. You ensure that materials, raw materials, and finished products are available at the right place and at the right time.

You will work from Monday to Friday, from 07:00 to 16:00, in a close-knit team of colleagues. Order, overview, and safety are central to your daily tasks.

As a Logistics Employee, your tasks include:

- Loading and unloading goods using a forklift;

- Receiving and assisting drivers (first point of contact);

- Packing and preparing finished products for shipment;

- Managing internal logistics between the warehouse and production departments;

- Supplying raw materials to various production departments;

- Cleaning and organizing the warehouse and production halls;

- Ensuring a safe and tidy workplace.

Requirements

- You work in a structured manner and have an eye for order and safety;

- You hold a valid forklift certificate;

- You are a true team player;

- You have a good command of the Dutch or English language.

As a Production Employee at Bavaria in Lieshout, you will play an important role in brewing and packaging one of the Netherlands' most iconic beers. In our state-of-the-art bottling facility, you help fill approximately 100,000 cans and bottles every hour.

Working at Bavaria means being involved in the entire production process. Together with your colleagues, you ensure that production runs as smoothly and efficiently as possible. Your shift starts and ends with a handover, where you discuss production results, breakdowns, and other important details with operators from the other teams.

At Bavaria, you will enjoy a varied role with responsibilities including:

- Setting up and adjusting machines;
- Troubleshooting common technical issues;
- Performing maintenance on the production line;
- Sorting returnable bottles;
- Supplying packaging machines with caps and rolls;
- Monitoring and checking beer quality.

Working Hours & Availability

Until January, you will work in a fixed 3-shift rotation with a repeating three-week cycle:

- Week 1: 4 to 5 night shifts from 10:00 PM to 06:00 AM
- Week 2: 3 afternoon shifts from 02:00 PM to 10:00 PM and 2 morning shifts from 06:00 AM to 02:00 PM
- Week 3: 3 morning shifts from 06:00 AM to 02:00 PM and 2 afternoon shifts from 02:00 PM to 10:00 PM

From January onwards, you will transition to a fixed 5-shift rotation schedule:

- 2 early shifts from 06:00 AM to 02:00 PM
- 2 late shifts from 02:00 PM to 10:00 PM
- 2 night shifts from 10:00 PM to 06:00 AM
- 4 days off

Are you ready to become part of this dynamic family-owned company? Apply now and you could soon be working in the bottling facility of Royal Swinkels!

- You are available to work in a 5-shift rotation schedule and till januari in a 3-shift schedule; 
- You have a good command of either the Dutch or English language;
- You are eager to learn and develop new skills.
